{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21879422",
      "title": "Organizing Route Files",
      "lectureOrder": 190,
      "videoOrder": 166,
      "sourceHash": "ecdcd7a41abc35001f8587d4ed866e45e34a7f3a29fbe0916f0e343703f2ac1d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.18,
          "end": 4.04,
          "en": "Now we know all the core",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.04,
          "end": 6.82,
          "en": "and even some advanced features which you need to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.82,
          "end": 9.78,
          "en": "about the Vue Router and about routing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.78,
          "end": 12.36,
          "en": "And we saw all those important features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.36,
          "end": 14.96,
          "en": "in action in this demo project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.96,
          "end": 19.43,
          "en": "Now we're going to build a bigger project in the next module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.43,
          "end": 22.58,
          "en": "where all of that makes even a bit more sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.58,
          "end": 25.59,
          "en": "since we'll then have a more realistic project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.59,
          "end": 27.58,
          "en": "Before we go there though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.58,
          "end": 32.58,
          "en": "let's talk about organizing our different files and folders,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.24,
          "end": 36.61,
          "en": "because at the moment I'm working with the components folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.61,
          "end": 39.57,
          "en": "with my different feature areas",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.57,
          "end": 43.4,
          "en": "and then the different components, nothing wrong with that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.4,
          "end": 46.75,
          "en": "But when you use routing, you could also argue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.75,
          "end": 48.99,
          "en": "that you don't just want to have components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.99,
          "end": 53.47,
          "en": "but maybe also a pages or a screens folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.47,
          "end": 55.67,
          "en": "And I'll go with pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.67,
          "end": 56.76,
          "en": "This is optional.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.76,
          "end": 57.98,
          "en": "You don't need that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.98,
          "end": 60.46,
          "en": "but you could then put the components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.46,
          "end": 63.52,
          "en": "which are loaded as pages through your router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.52,
          "end": 67.68,
          "en": "into the pages folder to have a clear distinction",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.68,
          "end": 71.7,
          "en": "between the components which are loaded through the router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.7,
          "end": 73.56,
          "en": "and the regular components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.56,
          "end": 75.87,
          "en": "which you embed in your templates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.87,
          "end": 78.21000000000001,
          "en": "Maybe you don't want this distinction.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.21000000000001,
          "end": 81.32,
          "en": "For team members, we for example ensured",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.32,
          "end": 84.43,
          "en": "that route parents are passed in as prompts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.43,
          "end": 86.03999999999999,
          "en": "So maybe that should be usable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.03999999999999,
          "end": 88.77,
          "en": "as a regular component as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.77,
          "end": 91.17,
          "en": "but maybe you do want this distinction.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.17,
          "end": 94.59,
          "en": "And then, of course, we could move Users List Vue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.59,
          "end": 96.52000000000001,
          "en": "and Teams List Vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 96.52000000000001,
          "end": 101.52000000000001,
          "en": "and also the Not Found page over into the pages folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.99000000000001,
          "end": 106.63,
          "en": "and also adds to Users Footer and the Teams Footer diary.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.63,
          "end": 107.62,
          "en": "And it's up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.62,
          "end": 110.463,
          "en": "whether you also want to use Team Members or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.36,
          "end": 115.41,
          "en": "Now we just need to update all the imports",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.41,
          "end": 118.863,
          "en": "and import team's list from pages/TeamsList,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 121.07,
          "end": 126.07,
          "en": "users list from pages/UsersList and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.56,
          "end": 129.03,
          "en": "Do that for all those pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 129.03,
          "end": 131.38,
          "en": "And again, this is really optional,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.38,
          "end": 134.35,
          "en": "but it can make sense especially in bigger apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.35,
          "end": 136.32999999999998,
          "en": "since it makes it easier to see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.32999999999998,
          "end": 139.54,
          "en": "which components will be loaded as pages through the router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.54,
          "end": 142.68,
          "en": "and which components will be used as components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.68,
          "end": 146.153,
          "en": "that are embedded into other components templates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.64,
          "end": 150.38,
          "en": "Now, with that you don't just need to update all the imports",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 150.38,
          "end": 152.24,
          "en": "in the main JS file, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.24,
          "end": 154.15,
          "en": "but also any imports you have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.15,
          "end": 156.5,
          "en": "inside all of your page components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 156.5,
          "end": 159.3,
          "en": "because here the POS are now incorrect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 159.3,
          "end": 163.07999999999998,
          "en": "We need to go up one level with two dots and a slash,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 163.07999999999998,
          "end": 165.25,
          "en": "then go into the Components folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 165.25,
          "end": 170.25,
          "en": "and then here into Users, UserItem.vue for teams list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 170.48,
          "end": 173.02,
          "en": "I also need to update teams item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 173.02,
          "end": 175.13,
          "en": "which I get from components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 175.13,
          "end": 178.69,
          "en": "So going up on level of components, teams,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 178.69,
          "end": 180.793,
          "en": "and TeamsTtem.vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 182.3,
          "end": 186.15,
          "en": "And with that that re-compiles and works as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 186.15,
          "end": 190.24,
          "en": "but now the pages are organized in a separate folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 190.24,
          "end": 192.07,
          "en": "Again, it's up to you whether you want this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 192.07,
          "end": 194.27,
          "en": "but I want to show this possible way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 194.27,
          "end": 195.993,
          "en": "of organizing components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 198.71,
          "end": 202.56,
          "en": "Now related to reorganizing our files and folders,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 202.56,
          "end": 206.34,
          "en": "you might notice that the main JS file gets rather big",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 206.34,
          "end": 208.32,
          "en": "with all our routes in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 208.32,
          "end": 211.37,
          "en": "Now this is of course a small app but even with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 211.37,
          "end": 215.71,
          "en": "all the routing logic takes up quite a bit of space in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 215.71,
          "end": 217.81,
          "en": "Now this is not bad per se,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 217.81,
          "end": 220.9,
          "en": "but it makes it harder to find the place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 220.9,
          "end": 224.11,
          "en": "where you actually create your app and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 224.11,
          "end": 228.12,
          "en": "Hence you might wanna use a separate router JS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 228.12,
          "end": 231.29,
          "en": "and actually move all the routing related code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 231.29,
          "end": 232.65,
          "en": "into that file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 232.65,
          "end": 237.31,
          "en": "So grab all that code here and move it into router JS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 237.31,
          "end": 239.543,
          "en": "except for the app Import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 240.6,
          "end": 244.69,
          "en": "And in main JS now get rid of all those other imports",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 245.63,
          "end": 247.5,
          "en": "and then take the router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 248.73,
          "end": 253.4,
          "en": "and all the routing logic catted from main JS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 253.4,
          "end": 256.29,
          "en": "and added here in router JS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 256.29,
          "end": 260.84,
          "en": "And then at the very bottom, export to router as a default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 261.9,
          "end": 264.8,
          "en": "so that we can import it into another file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 264.8,
          "end": 268.04,
          "en": "because we need to import it into main JS now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 268.04,
          "end": 271.913,
          "en": "We can import a router from ./outer.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 272.96,
          "end": 276.13,
          "en": "and then we can still use router because we're importing it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 276.13,
          "end": 278.913,
          "en": "But with that, everything will work as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 278.913,
          "end": 282.6,
          "en": "but our routing code is now in a separate file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 282.6,
          "end": 284.89,
          "en": "and that makes our code overall",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 284.89,
          "end": 287.33299999999997,
          "en": "more manageable and maintainable.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
